# Accessibility Rule

Apply this rule for UI, forms, navigation, and interactive behavior changes.

## Required Checks

- All controls must have accessible names and semantic roles.
- Keyboard navigation must work for all interactive elements.
- Focus states must be visible and logical.
- Color contrast and text readability must meet WCAG targets.
- Form fields need labels, validation cues, and clear error messages.
- Dynamic content updates should be announced appropriately when needed.

## Implementation Guidance

- Prefer native HTML semantics before custom ARIA.
- Use ARIA only to supplement, not replace, proper semantics.
- Avoid click-only interaction patterns; support keyboard activation.
